# modules/iac/helm.rules - Helm chart checks, scoped to values.yaml/templates/*.yaml.
# precision.awk checks literal Pod fields by ownership. Values without a
# rendered workload remain informational review because their use is unknown.
# File references are not literal credential values.
# Owns: docs/DESIGN.md §6.6/§8.2; docs/FOUNDATION.md tension 3 precision amendment.

id: IAC-HELM-HOST_PORT-01
title: Container port published directly on the host network via hostPort
severity: high
confidence: high
cwe: CWE-668
owasp: A02:2025
pattern: hostPort\s*:\s*[0-9]+
dialect: ere
files: values.yaml
files: templates/*.yaml
context-deny: ^\s*#\s*scoursh-allow: host-port
context-window: 1
tags: static
tags: compliance
remediation: Remove hostPort (or the NodePort service type it typically pairs with) and reach
  the workload through a ClusterIP Service plus an Ingress/LoadBalancer instead. hostPort binds
  the container port directly onto every node's host network interface, bypassing the cluster's
  own network policy and exposing the port to anything that can reach the node.
references: CWE-668

id: IAC-HELM-HOST_MOUNT-01
title: hostPath volume mounts a sensitive host directory into the container
severity: critical
confidence: medium
cwe: CWE-668
owasp: A02:2025
pattern: path\s*:\s*["']?(/etc|/var/run/docker\.sock|/root|/proc|/sys|/home)\b
dialect: ere
files: values.yaml
files: templates/*.yaml
tags: static
tags: compliance
remediation: Remove the hostPath volume and use a PersistentVolumeClaim, ConfigMap, or Secret
  instead. Mounting /var/run/docker.sock hands the container the equivalent of root on the host
  (full control of the container runtime); mounting /etc, /root, /proc, /sys, or /home exposes
  host secrets, credentials, or kernel/process state to anything running in the pod.
references: CWE-668

id: IAC-HELM-HARDCODED_SECRET-01
title: Plaintext credential literal in a Helm chart
severity: critical
confidence: medium
cwe: CWE-798
owasp: A07:2025
# Matching is line-oriented; use POSIX bracket classes without backslash escapes.
pattern: \b(password|secret|secretKey|secret_key|apiKey|api_key|access_key|token|clientSecret)\b[[:space:]]*:[[:space:]]*["']?[^"'[:space:]{][^"']{7,}
dialect: ere
files: values.yaml
files: templates/*.yaml
context-deny: (CHANGEME|changeme|EXAMPLE|example|XXXXXXXX|xxxxxxxx|placeholder|dummy|TODO)
# Not literals: prose in a comment (`# password: Password for the admin
# user`), a Go-template variable (`{{- $password := include ... }}` reads as
# `password:` to the pattern), a `$`-reference, any `{{` template, and the
# `my-password` docs placeholder.  Whitespace inside `[...]` is spelled
# `[:space:]`: `grep -E` reads a backslash there as a literal byte, so a
# bracketed shorthand matches differently under the two engines.
context-deny: \b(password|secret|secretKey|secret_key|apiKey|api_key|access_key|token|clientSecret)\b\s*:\s*["']?[^"'[:space:]{][^"'[:space:]]*[[:space:]]+[^#[:space:]]
context-deny: \$[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*[[:space:]]*:=
context-deny: \b(password|secret|secretKey|secret_key|apiKey|api_key|access_key|token|clientSecret)\b\s*:\s*["']?\$
context-deny: \{\{
context-deny: \b(password|secret|secretKey|secret_key|apiKey|api_key|access_key|token|clientSecret)\b\s*:\s*["']?[Mm][Yy][-_]?([Ss][Ee][Cc][Rr][Ee][Tt]|[Pp][Aa][Ss][Ss]|[Tt][Oo][Kk][Ee][Nn])
context-window: 0
tags: static
remediation: Remove the literal credential from values.yaml/templates and rotate it immediately;
  a committed secret must be treated as compromised even if the commit is later reverted, because
  it remains in git history. Source the value from an existing Kubernetes Secret via
  valueFrom.secretKeyRef (or an external-secrets operator backed by Vault/AWS Secrets Manager/SSM
  SecureString) instead of a literal in values.yaml or a template.
references: CWE-798
